@sofiandrade requested your review on: #414 Dedupe events by (site, line, ts).

When a gateway reconnects it replays its buffer, and we were storing the replayed events twice. This adds a unique index on (site_id, line_id, ts, seq) and makes the writer an upsert. Includes a one-off migration that removes the existing duplicates (about 0.3% of rows on prod, almost all from gateway reconnects).

Migration is idempotent and runs in batches of 10k.

